       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so the effects could last for days.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Common intended doses are:\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a typical starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for frail or older patients or those with hepatic impairment\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
